.TH XCALC 1 2026-11-20 __xorgversion__
.SH NAME
xcalc \- scientific calculator for X
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xcalc
[\fB\-\-mode\fP=\fImode\fP] [\fB\-\-rpn\fP] [\fB\-\-theme\fP=\fItheme\fP]
.br
.B xcalc \-\-help
.br
.B xcalc \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I xcalc
is a calculator with a modern GTK3 interface.  It is built on the original
\fIxcalc\fP math engine, which emulates the TI\-30 (algebraic notation) and
the HP\-10C (reverse Polish notation).
.PP
Four modes are available from the drop\-down in the header bar:
.TP 8
.B Standard
Basic arithmetic, backspace and memory keys.
.TP 8
.B Scientific
Adds trigonometry, logarithms, powers, factorial, constants and parentheses.
The \fBINV\fP key switches the labels of \fBsin\fP, \fBcos\fP, \fBtan\fP,
\fBlog\fP and \fBln\fP to their inverse functions.  \fBDEG\fP cycles between
degrees, radians and grads.
.TP 8
.B Programmer
Hexadecimal, decimal and octal entry, and the bitwise operators
AND, OR, XOR, NOT and the left and right shifts.  Digits that are not valid in
the current base are disabled.
.TP 8
.B RPN (HP\-10C)
Reverse Polish notation with the \fBENTER\fP key and the HP stack
operations.  Memory is addressed with \fBSTO\fP, \fBRCL\fP and \fBSUM\fP followed
by a digit from 0 to 9.
.PP
The display shows up to 12 significant digits.  The small line above the number
shows the expression being entered.  The menu in the header bar selects the
light, dark or system appearance, copies the result, pastes a number and shows
the about dialog.
.SH OPTIONS
Both the \-\- and the single dash forms are accepted.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-mode= mode
Start in \fImode\fP, one of \fBstandard\fP, \fBscientific\fP,
\fBprogrammer\fP or \fBrpn\fP.  The last mode used is remembered.
.TP 8
.B \-\-rpn
Same as \fB\-\-mode=rpn\fP.  This is the old option of the Xaw version.
.TP 8
.BI \-\-theme= theme
Use the \fBsystem\fP, \fBlight\fP or \fBdark\fP appearance.  The choice is
remembered.
.TP 8
.B \-\-help
Print a usage message and exit.
.TP 8
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
The standard GTK options (for example \fB\-\-display\fP) are also understood.
The old \fB\-stipple\fP option is accepted and ignored.
.SH KEYBOARD
The calculator can be driven entirely from the keyboard.
.TP 8
.B 0\-9 . , + \- * / =
Digits, decimal point and the basic operators.
.TP 8
.B Enter
Equals; in RPN mode, ENTER.
.TP 8
.B BackSpace
Erase the last digit.
.TP 8
.B Escape
Clear the entry; press twice to clear everything (the \fBC\fP key).
.TP 8
.B Delete
All clear, including memory (the \fBAC\fP key).
.TP 8
.B ^ ! % ( )
Power, factorial, modulus and parentheses (Scientific and Programmer modes).
.TP 8
.B n
Change sign.
.TP 8
.B s c t l g r p e i d
Scientific mode: sin, cos, tan, ln, log, square root, pi, e, INV and DEG.
.TP 8
.B a\-f x & | < > ~
Programmer mode: hexadecimal digits, XOR, AND, OR, shift left, shift right and
NOT.
.TP 8
.B F5 F6 F7
Programmer mode: hexadecimal, decimal and octal.
.TP 8
.B Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V, Ctrl+Q
Copy the result, paste a number, quit.
.SH FILES
.TP 8
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xcalc/settings.ini
Remembered mode and appearance (normally \fI~/.config/xcalc/settings.ini\fP).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP 8
.B DISPLAY
The X server to connect to.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR X (__miscmansuffix__)
.SH BUGS
The engine keeps the behaviour of the original program, so some old quirks
remain: for example \fBINV\fP followed by \fBx\(S2\fP takes a square root, and
the modulus and the bitwise operators work on the integer part of the numbers.
.PP
Please report problems at
\fIhttps://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/app/xcalc/\-/issues\fP for the engine,
or in the issue tracker of the project that ships this GTK3 front\-end.
